    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The problem is the marketing budget is already tied to the 'comfort' angle. If we scale back to just 'rapid action', the projected ROI drops significantly and the whole project might get downgraded by the board. \n\nIs there any way we could frame the nausea data differently? Like, if we characterize it as a 'transient' or 'manageable' effect, could we still keep the 'superior comfort' messaging in the campaign without it looking like we're dodging the clinical findings?",
